DS3D LiDAR file writer is an implementation of `ds3d::datarender` which writes
the point cloud and the 3D detection results from a `ds3d::datamap` out to files
instead of drawing them. It is the headless counterpart of the GL render modules
and is the sink of choice for batch runs, regression checks and machines without
a display. It is the write-side mirror of the `ds3d/dataloader/lidarsource`
reader.

DS3D is framework agnostic. There is no gstreamer/Glib dependencies. Any framework could
simply wrap DS3D modules.

`libnvds_lidarfilewrite.so` is built from these source files. and the LiDAR file
render is created through API `createLidarFileDataRender`. Application users can
call this API to instantiate this datarender.

In compatible with Gstreamer plugins, `ds3d::datarender` could be loaded into GstAppSink
in runtime through API `NvDs3D_CreateDataRenderSink(config)`
The config content shall as:

    type: ds3d::datarender
    in_caps: ds3d/datamap
    custom_lib_path: libnvds_lidarfilewrite.so
    custom_create_function: createLidarFileDataRender
    config_body:
       ...

Any custom `ds3d::datarender` must derive from `ds3d::BaseImplDataRender` for data rendering
And implement the following interfaces:

    ErrCode startImpl(const std::string& content, const std::string& path) override;
    ErrCode prerollImpl(GuardDataMap datamap) override;
    ErrCode renderImpl(GuardDataMap datamap, OnGuardDataCBImpl dataDoneCb) override;
    ErrCode stopImpl() override;
    ErrCode flushImpl() override;

In addition, users also need export a C-API for application to intiate this datarender.
The exported C-API name is not limited. In this sample, it is `createLidarFileDataRender`.

More details, refer to the DeepStream SDK documentation for section of "DeepStream 3D Custom Manual".
https://nvidia-deepstream.docs.buildwithfern.com/deepstream/9.2/text/DS_3D_Custom_Manual

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Pre-requisites:
- libnvds_3d_common.so (build and install ds3d/common first)
- libyaml-cpp Development package
- CUDA Runtime

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Compiling and installing this `ds3d::datarender` lib:
- Export CUDA_VER, then build. sudo -E keeps the variable for make.
  $ export CUDA_VER=13.2 # x86, Jetson and SBSA. For IGX Thor, CUDA_VER=13.0
  $ make && sudo -E make install
- Verify `libnvds_lidarfilewrite.so` exist and installed well.

NOTE: Compiling does not need root. Install with `sudo -E` so CUDA_VER is kept. Skip sudo when already root (for example inside a container).
